<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24138" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">intensĭo</span></b> , ōnis,
			f.
		intendo. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A stretching out</i>, <i>straining</i>, <i>effort</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oculorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Scrib. Comp. 255</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>An intensifying</i>, <i>increase</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">calorem suum (sol) intensionibus ac
					remissionibus temperando fovet,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Q. N. 7, 1, 3</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>The tune</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gravis, media, acuta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Censor. 12</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
